(D5 - Discrepancy 5 repro, RESOLVED by vox #279 (register #135, #136).
 Up to vox 0.4.15 `Send signal` handed the pid straight to kill(2), so
 pid 0 (the caller's process group) and pid -1 (every process this uid may
 signal) were reachable with no diagnostic, and this probe printed
 "kill(2) accepted the broadcast pid".
 Now `to process <pid>` reaches exactly one process, numbered 1 to
 2147483647 (LANGUAGE.md:4584, 4593-4597), and a pid the compiler can
 prove is outside that range is a compile error whose help line names the
 group forms. `Send signal 0 to process 0.` is refused the same way. A pid
 known only at run time is refused when the program runs: PRC-77.vox.
 SAFETY: signal 0 only, and the program no longer compiles.
 Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D5.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: cannot send a signal to process -1
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
Send signal 0 to process -1.
On error print "pid -1 was rejected".
print "kill(2) accepted the broadcast pid".
